1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.950
I grabbed hold, digging in my claws
te ni totte tsume o tateta

3
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.380
but the future
sono mirai wa

4
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:34.600
blurred together, colors running
nijimu iro ni kasunde mieta

5
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:41.200
A red that can swallow even summer's hues
natsu no iro mo nuritsubusu you na aka ni

6
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:47.920
bokura no koe kakikesareteiku you de
now attempts to blot out our voices

7
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:54.660
Move those halting feet of yours
tachidomaru sono ashi o fumidasou ze

8
00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:01.300
Don't let stand the lies for show
misekake no uso yarisugosu yori

9
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:07.550
I'll give up countless mornings for my vows
nandome no asa chikai to hikikaeru yo

10
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:16.100
For the dream that we shared
bokura ga miteita yume

11
00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:33.070
Navy HQ
New World

12
00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.680
What?!

13
00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:35.470
The world’s going to
sink into the sea?!

14
00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:39.060
What are you even
talking about, Dr. Vegapunk?!

15
00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:45.790
Mock 
Town, 
Town of Ridicule

16
00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.190
This guy’s a riot!

17
00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:54.320
Takin’ advantage of his own death,
usin’ it to try to cause mayhem in the world!

18
00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.790
How’s it even possible
for the whole world to go under?!

19
00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:05.080
If you’re gonna lie,
at least make it believable!

20
00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:08.320
City of
Water
Water Seven

21
00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:14.000
I’d believe him if he was only talking about our country,

22
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.510
where the land’s been sinking in deeper every year...

23
00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:22.770
But the whole damn world?

24
00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:26.350
It’s not just a matter of
high tide and low tide, is it?

25
00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:33.720
Impel Down,
the Under-
water
Prison

26
00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:36.240
Man, don’t you just love this?

27
00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:40.950
If Impel Down floods,
what’re you gonna do about it?

28
00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:45.420
It’s your job to
keep the prisoners safe, isn’t it,

29
00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:47.380
Magellan?

30
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.260
Indeed,

31
00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:58.140
the whole place went into panic
when the sea level rose by a meter the other day.

32
00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:03.220
How many meters will it be,
should the entire world go under?

33
00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:16.150
A five-meter rise
would destroy most cities.

34
00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.700
Think we oughta move?

35
00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.830
To much higher ground?!

36
00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.780
Ryugu Kingdom
Fishman Island

37
00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:40.470
Father...

38
00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:43.310
What do you think will happen?

39
00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:47.270
It baffles the mind, jamon.

40
00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:53.820
What is he saying?!

41
00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:58.800
Future Island
Egghead

42
00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:56.440
He’s the world’s greatest scientist!

43
00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:58.820
He can wreak havoc on the world,
even with a lie!

44
00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:02.120
It’s total nonsense!

45
00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:07.430
<b>The Wings of Icarus</b>

46
00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.580
Dr. Vegapunk!

47
00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:11.170
Destroy the Transmission Transponder Snail!

48
00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:15.000
No, destroy all life forms
you can hear!

49
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.550
All other concerns are secondary!

50
00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:37.940
Come on!

51
00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:39.900
Just how much’re you
gonna give away?!

52
00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.120
Stella!

53
00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:50.460
This will be a bit in the future
 from where I’m standing,

54
00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:53.670
but mere days
 after I make this recording,

55
00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:57.630
assuming the sensor I created
 and my calculations are right,

56
00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:02.590
an unusual earthquake
 will shake the entire world.

57
00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:03.930
Uh?

58
00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.270
Is that about today’s earthquake?!

59
00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:10.230
But Vegapunk’s
supposed to be dead by now!

60
00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:12.440
Then...

61
00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:20.150
Then as a result, the sea levels will rise
 by approximately one meter around the world,

62
00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:23.410
and some islands are certain
 to become uninhabitable!

63
00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:24.820
Eh? Is this a prophecy?

64
00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.290
As such, the loss of numerous beaches
 around the world would be inevitable.

65
00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:33.210
If this turns out to be incorrect,

66
00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:36.880
feel free to ignore
 everything else I tell you.

67
00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:40.840
How?! This is creepy, man!
He got it all right!

68
00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:44.550
But if it does happen,

69
00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:49.220
pay very close attention
 to what I’m about to say!

70
00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:55.520
That earthquake is the furthest possible thing
 from a natural phenomenon!

71
00:05:57.770 --> 00:06:00.530
Vegapunk!

72
00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:04.740
You will not speak another word!

73
00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:06.870
Zeus!

74
00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:16.790
Aubade Coup Droit!

75
00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:25.180
Bubble Gun!

76
00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:29.970
Just go away!

77
00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.410
I...

78
00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.880
I, in my own humble way...

79
00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:02.840
...wished for peace...

80
00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:10.100
You damned insects!

81
00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:25.110
Cien Fleurs:

82
00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:28.570
Spider Net!

83
00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:38.170
Get out of my way!

84
00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:41.040
Huh?

85
00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:11.120
Mars, have you checked
the power plant?

86
00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:12.200
Not yet.

87
00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:15.540
That room, more so than any others,
must remain intact.

88
00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:17.200
I will go!

89
00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:26.880
Yes... I wished for peace
 in my own humble way...

90
00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.800
But that was...

91
00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:32.390
...my first crime.

92
00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:35.140
I dreamed of unlimited energy...

93
00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:38.520
Driven by...

94
00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:43.520
Driven by a desire
 to bring major progress to the world...

95
00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:56.450
The Mother Flame!

96
00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:59.390
Mother Flame

97
00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:14.850
I flew...

98
00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:18.060
...too close to the sun.

99
00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:22.060
This is not it, either!

100
00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:25.310
Slaughter every living thing in the lab!

101
00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:35.370
I’m going to explain, in order,

102
00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:43.580
the events about
 to take place in our world.

103
00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:45.630
No luck! Not even a dent!

104
00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:48.920
What is that thing?
It’s not even flinching!

105
00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:53.050
Hotowowowow!

106
00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:59.010
Hey! You’re gonna be burned to a crisp!
Get moving!

107
00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:09.190
This is about the century
roughly between 900 to 800 years ago.

108
00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:16.200
There is a void in history
around that period of time.

109
00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:20.370
Hey, Marines! What are you even doing-eh?!

110
00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:22.830
Shut him up already!

111
00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:25.790
It is referred to as the Void Century,

112
00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:29.000
and it has been erased from history.

113
00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:33.630
The death penalty is not enough!
Present his corpse! I’ll chop it into pieces!

114
00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.630
The Void Century?

115
00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:37.760
I must say, what might that be?

116
00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:40.970
The only way to learn about
 that period of time...

117
00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:45.560
...is to decipher the letters from the past
 called Poneglyphs...

118
00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:48.730
...which are scattered
 all over the world.

119
00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:55.090
Orange
Town,

East
Blue

120
00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:55.110
Well, long, long ago

121
00:10:55.090 --> 00:11:01.930
WORLD

122
00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:58.410
There were 20 kings who got together

123
00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:00.450
and they created the world!

124
00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:03.500
Doesn’t that old guy know that?

125
00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:06.290
What do you think, Chouchou?

126
00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:14.800
Deciphering Poneglyphs is strictly prohibited
 by the World Government,

127
00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:20.350
but despite being a Government scientist,
 I tried my hand at it.

128
00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:21.390
That’s my...

129
00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:23.850
...second crime.

130
00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:30.060
I studied books that some brilliant archaeologists
 preserved through sheer tenacity,

131
00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:33.480
deciphered a number of Poneglyphs,

132
00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:36.570
and pushed the research
as far as I could.

133
00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:39.530
I bear not even the slightest regret!

134
00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:43.990
History, you see, tells a story!

135
00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:50.830
But all I have learned...

136
00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:53.550
...is an incomplete story of that century.

137
00:11:54.050 --> 00:11:57.720
Filling in the gaps with my own speculations
 would be inappropriate,

138
00:11:57.720 --> 00:12:01.640
so I’ll pass on to you
 only the facts I’m sure of.

139
00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:14.190
Hey! Don’t even bother tryin’, Straw Hat!

140
00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:18.650
The protagonist of this story...

141
00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:24.280
...is a man, born 900 years ago
 in an impossibly advanced kingdom.

142
00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:30.580
This oughta do it!

143
00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:35.590
Like the Sun God Nika
spoken of in the Elbaph legend...

144
00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:39.010
...he fought with a stretchy, elastic body.

145
00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:52.020
His name was Joyboy.

146
00:12:57.070 --> 00:13:00.450
Ow, ow, hothothot...!
Ooh, yow, ow, hooot...!

147
00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:03.200
Stop tryin’ to make us laugh!

148
00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:08.450
You never learn!

149
00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:10.960
It burrrrns!

150
00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:13.210
He was the very first man
 in this world of the sea...

151
00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:16.710
...to be called a pirate.

152
00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:25.910
Flower Capital














Land of Wano

153
00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:25.930
Joyboy...

154
00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:29.770
Why was he called a pirate?

155
00:13:29.770 --> 00:13:34.560
Hmm... It is surprising that external signals
are being received within this country.

156
00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:39.530
Orochi had it at the castle,
and it really came in handy!

157
00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:42.490
So Joyboy was a pirate...

158
00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:44.660
He sounds just like Luffy.

159
00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:47.530
Do you know of Joyboy, my Lord?

160
00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:50.250
Big Bro Luffy...

161
00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:53.080
I wanna see him again soon!

162
00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:56.590
Aye, me too.

163
00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:06.240
Naval Branch G-4















Prison

164
00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:08.720
Joyboy?

165
00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:11.770
Is he stronger than our captain?

166
00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:14.440
No way, right? Captain Kid.

167
00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:16.940
Go easy on him...

168
00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:18.360
He’s already dead.

169
00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:21.380
Former Fake Luffy









Demalo Black

170
00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:24.950
That’s our Big Boss Kid!
You gots a big heart.

171
00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:26.820
So handsome!

172
00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:32.250
Of course he was weaker than me!

173
00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:33.580
Joyball!

174
00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:37.580
Uh... I think it’s “boy”.

175
00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:41.300
Joy... boy?

176
00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:44.880
I’ve only read a handful of Poneglyphs,

177
00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:50.350
but what was inscribed on them
 was a record of a great war.

178
00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:55.390
Joyboy fought against
 the World Government of today.

179
00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:57.850
Huh? Does he mean us?

180
00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:00.820
Well, if he was a pirate...

181
00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.650
Vegapunk!

182
00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:07.610
To be more precise, it was
the precursor of the World Government,

183
00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:10.280
the temporary coalition
 consisting of twenty kingdoms,

184
00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:11.910
known as the Alliance!

185
00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:27.090
It could be argued that Joyboy’s faction
was so strong that it compelled them to join forces.

186
00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:32.350
Without knowing the spark that caused the war,

187
00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:37.310
I’ll call it a clash of ideologies,
rather than a matter of good and evil.

188
00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:47.430
Zou,
New
World

189
00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:45.190
As I mentioned earlier,
the country of Joyboy’s birth...

190
00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:51.620
...had a civilization unbelievably
 advanced for its time 900 years ago.

191
00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:56.000
Joyboy...

192
00:15:57.040 --> 00:16:00.330
I wonder if he had some
connection with Zunesha.

193
00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:04.210
The weapons that existed
 during that century-long war...

194
00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:09.630
...were apparently beyond the capacity of
 modern science to create.

195
00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:10.930
That’s amazing!

196
00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:16.810
What’re you going on about,

197
00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:18.730
you peanutty idiot!

198
00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:22.150
Oh, no!

199
00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:25.150
Boss, forget that nonsense. I’m hungry!

200
00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:28.190
Nonsense?!

201
00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:32.410
Not even a genius like me
 could replicate them!

202
00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:34.990
That’s not something to brag about,
you moron!

203
00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:39.830
Yes...

204
00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:42.440
That’s where...

205
00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:45.170
...the problem lies.

206
00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:51.180
Zoro-san! Jinbe-san!

207
00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:53.640
Ow, ow, ow...

208
00:16:57.930 --> 00:16:58.810
Wait a minute!

209
00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:00.230
It’s moving!

210
00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:03.730
Look! Aren’t the clouds stretching?!

211
00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:05.900
They are!

212
00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:07.940
But why are they?

213
00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:13.410
Is this what Edison-san meant when he said
he’d help us land on the water safely?

214
00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:14.160
Ah!

215
00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:18.370
You’re right! If the clouds stretch out,
we can reach the sea!

216
00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:21.750
Now we can make our getaway!

217
00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:22.580
Yes!

218
00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:24.330
Yay!

219
00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:26.290
Edison...

220
00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:39.060
Y’all gotta get outta here
no matter what, Straw Hats!

221
00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:47.440
Dun let da World Government...

222
00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:51.150
...catch y’all!

223
00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:07.780
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop, beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop
Piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipapii papipo, piipapii

224
00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:12.000
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop beep-beep-beep-bup-bop
Piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipii pipopii, pipopiipii

225
00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:16.210
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop, beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop
Piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipapii papipo, piipapii

226
00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:18.690
Beep-bup-beep
Piipapii papipo, piipapii

227
00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:23.740
No No No No No norenai

228
00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:23.820
No, no, no, no, no, not feelin' it

229
00:18:23.820 --> 00:18:27.980
kobiritsuichatte mou odorenai

230
00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:28.020
I'm all stiff, all outta dances

231
00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:32.260
My head feels so good, 'f I get unlucky again
atama Feel so good, mata Unlucky demo

232
00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:36.360
Cola de fukitobase yowaki o
just gonna blow away the shy with a cola

233
00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:40.440
Hey all you boys & girls! Looking good!
soko no Boys & Girls! omae ii yatsu

234
00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:43.990
Hey all you boys & girls!
soko no Boys & Girls!

235
00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:47.960
Update failed. I've had enough!
appudeto wa shippai kori gori

236
00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:49.840
Wasn't it OK 'til yesterday?
kinou made nara seikai?

237
00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:56.170
La la la la la la, run, run, run...
ran ran ran ran ran ran Run Run Run

238
00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:59.890
"Hiding yet?"
mou ii kai?

239
00:18:59.890 --> 00:19:02.260
You ready yet, up for a dance
junbi wa douyo odoreru no?

240
00:19:02.260 --> 00:19:04.630
bukkowareteru kono jidai
in this broken era?

241
00:19:04.630 --> 00:19:08.310
"Come find us!"
mou ii yo!

242
00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:10.660
Spread out from here, drop into the world
koko kara kakusan sekai e Drop

243
